  "category": "Source Control",
  "description": "A Git Hooks view with the repository's hooks (from core.hooksPath or .git/hooks, so Husky's .husky folder too): which are active, off or not executable. Click to open one; run it in a terminal with the arguments git gives it; turn it off and on (renamed to <hook>.off); make it executable; delete it. \"New Hook…\" writes one from a template: dotnet format check, dotnet build, dotnet test before a push, a Conventional Commits message check, the issue number from the branch name, dotnet restore after a pull, or an empty one. Husky.NET tasks (.husky/task-runner.json) are listed by group and run with dotnet husky run. Needs .NET 10 and git.",
  "runtime": "dotnet",
  "assembly": "bin/GitHooks.dll",
  "requires": ["git"],
